1
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:08,750
Hello to our lecturer, and hello everyone.

2
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:14,014
My name is Panhna. I am a student
at ACLEDA University of Business,

3
00:00:14,064 --> 00:00:17,550
majoring in Computer
Science and Engineering.

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:22,866
I am a member of Team 1.
Our team has four members:

5
00:00:22,916 --> 00:00:25,550
me, Bora, Raksa, and Mengkuang.

6
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:29,748
Today, we will present our study project,

7
00:00:29,798 --> 00:00:32,643
supervised by Lecturer Keo Tongheng.

8
00:00:32,693 --> 00:00:37,550
It is called the AI Chatbot
Management System (Telegram Bot).

9
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:45,134
This system answers students' frequent
questions right away, even at night,

10
00:00:45,184 --> 00:00:48,431
and it reduces the workload of staff.

11
00:00:48,481 --> 00:00:51,550
We hope you enjoy our presentation.

12
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:57,093
This is Sokha. She wants
to apply to a university,

13
00:00:57,143 --> 00:01:01,550
but she does not know
which documents she needs.

14
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:07,240
She sends a message to ask
about the application process

15
00:01:07,290 --> 00:01:09,550
and the required documents.

16
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:14,371
But it is already midnight.

17
00:01:14,421 --> 00:01:16,550
Nobody replies.

18
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:18,772
This is Dara.

19
00:01:18,822 --> 00:01:23,550
He works in customer
service at the university.

20
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:30,315
In the morning, when he arrives at
work, he finds many messages waiting.

21
00:01:30,365 --> 00:01:34,550
Most of them are the same
questions again and again.

22
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:38,232
He starts answering them

23
00:01:38,282 --> 00:01:40,550
one by one, by hand.

24
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:43,452
It takes a long time,

25
00:01:43,502 --> 00:01:45,550
and it is very tiring.

26
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:49,195
He thinks: “If only a program

27
00:01:49,245 --> 00:01:53,550
could answer these
repeated questions for me.”

28
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:59,838
So, we built the AI Chatbot
Management System (Telegram Bot).

29
00:01:59,888 --> 00:02:03,900
It has two parts: a
Telegram bot for students,

30
00:02:03,950 --> 00:02:06,550
and a web dashboard for staff.

31
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:11,408
In the dashboard, staff
can create, manage,

32
00:02:11,458 --> 00:02:15,550
and save frequently
asked questions, or FAQs.

33
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:19,094
The bot can handle questions

34
00:02:19,144 --> 00:02:21,550
in both Khmer and English.

35
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:26,038
It can understand questions
with the same meaning,

36
00:02:26,088 --> 00:02:28,550
even when they use different words.

37
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:35,221
If it cannot answer a
question, it says so honestly,

38
00:02:35,271 --> 00:02:39,550
and passes the conversation to a human.

39
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:43,201
So, students get answers right away,

40
00:02:43,251 --> 00:02:48,550
and staff no longer need to answer
the same questions again and again.

41
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:53,603
Sokha starts by sending /start,

42
00:02:53,653 --> 00:02:56,550
and she chooses Khmer.

43
00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:00,824
She asks the same question

44
00:03:00,874 --> 00:03:03,550
she asked last night.

45
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,614
The bot answers immediately,

46
00:03:06,664 --> 00:03:09,550
using an answer from the existing FAQ.

47
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:11,969
She taps 👍

48
00:03:12,019 --> 00:03:14,550
to give feedback.

49
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:18,047
She can also switch

50
00:03:18,097 --> 00:03:19,550
to English.

51
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:23,917
She asks the same question
in different words.

52
00:03:23,967 --> 00:03:30,550
The bot still understands, even though the
words are not the same as the saved question.

53
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:38,565
It can even find a date
in the conversation

54
00:03:38,615 --> 00:03:40,550
and save it.

55
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:41,993
Next,

56
00:03:42,043 --> 00:03:46,550
she asks a question the bot does not know.

57
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:50,084
The bot does not guess.

58
00:03:50,134 --> 00:03:54,550
It says sorry, and offers help options.

59
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:58,018
She chooses Human Support.

60
00:03:58,068 --> 00:04:03,550
With just one tap, her request
goes to the support team.

61
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:06,420
The next morning,

62
00:04:06,470 --> 00:04:09,550
Dara logs in to the system.

63
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:12,853
He sees the statistics

64
00:04:12,903 --> 00:04:17,550
and the questions the
bot could not answer.

65
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:20,078
Sokha's request

66
00:04:20,128 --> 00:04:23,550
is already waiting in his queue.

67
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:28,753
Here, he can read the whole conversation

68
00:04:28,803 --> 00:04:31,550
between Sokha and the bot.

69
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:34,429
He types a reply,

70
00:04:34,479 --> 00:04:39,550
and it arrives in
Telegram on Sokha's phone.

71
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:41,121
Then,

72
00:04:41,171 --> 00:04:45,550
he marks the request as Resolved.

73
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:48,700
Dara clicks Add FAQ.

74
00:04:48,750 --> 00:04:54,550
Sokha's question is already
filled in automatically.

75
00:04:55,500 --> 00:05:01,382
He only types the answer, with no
need to type the question again,

76
00:05:01,432 --> 00:05:02,550
and saves it.

77
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:08,456
Another student asks the same
thing in different words,

78
00:05:08,506 --> 00:05:10,550
and the bot can answer.

79
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:15,756
The question the bot could
not answer yesterday,

80
00:05:15,806 --> 00:05:17,550
it can answer today.

81
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:21,673
Dara can also send a message

82
00:05:21,723 --> 00:05:24,550
to all bot users at once.

83
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:29,000
He can export reports as PDF or Excel,

84
00:05:29,050 --> 00:05:32,550
and Khmer text is displayed correctly.

85
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:36,744
He can also set the permissions

86
00:05:36,794 --> 00:05:38,550
for each account.

87
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:44,215
A Viewer account only sees masked names,

88
00:05:44,265 --> 00:05:47,550
and it cannot open Settings.

89
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:52,181
Now, Sokha gets answers even at midnight,

90
00:05:52,231 --> 00:05:57,550
and Dara no longer copies the
same answers again and again.

91
00:05:58,500 --> 00:06:03,432
We tested the bot with 57
questions that our team wrote.

92
00:06:03,482 --> 00:06:07,258
It answered 53 correctly
and 4 incorrectly.

93
00:06:07,308 --> 00:06:10,550
That is about 92.98 percent accuracy.

94
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:16,730
These results come from
our own test questions,

95
00:06:16,780 --> 00:06:20,550
not from a large public benchmark.

96
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:25,132
Next, we will deploy the AI chatbot

97
00:06:25,182 --> 00:06:29,550
and test it with real university students.

98
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:33,898
This is the end of our presentation.

99
00:06:33,948 --> 00:06:39,550
Thank you, Lecturer, and thank
you, everyone, for watching.
